[TITLE:e200z6 Manual Extracted Data - Critical Specifications]

[INTRO]
This document contains key specifications extracted directly from the e200z6 Core
Reference Manual for validation against LLVM implementation.

MANUAL_SOURCE: https://www.elektronikjk.com/elementy_czynne/IC/E200Z6.pdf
EXTRACTION_DATE: 2025-11-02
EXTRACTION_METHOD: pdftotext + manual review

[CHAPTER-7-TIMING]
UID: CH7-TIMING

TITLE: Instruction Timing Specifications

LOCATION: Chapter 7.2.3 (Execution Units)

INTEGER_INSTRUCTIONS:
- Simple integer (adds, subtracts, compares, shifts, rotates, count leading zeros): 
  1 cycle latency, single cycle execution
  
- Multiply instructions: 
  Latency: 3 cycles
  Throughput: 1 per cycle (pipelined)
  
- Divide instructions:
  Latency: Variable 6-16 cycles (data-dependent)
  Worst case: 16 cycles
  Throughput: Blocking (pipeline unavailable during divide)

LOAD_STORE_INSTRUCTIONS:
- Load instructions:
  Latency: 3 cycles
  Throughput: 1 per cycle (maximum, pipelined)
  Note: Load followed by dependent instruction can be fed forward
  
- Store instructions:
  Latency: 3 cycles
  Throughput: 1 per cycle (maximum, pipelined)
  Store data can be fed-forward from immediately preceding load (no stall)

BRANCH_INSTRUCTIONS:
- Conditional branches (not taken): 1 clock cycle
- Taken branches: 3 clocks (branch target address calculated in parallel with decode)
- Branches with successful BTB target prefetching: 1 clock cycle (if correctly predicted)

FLOATING_POINT_INSTRUCTIONS (if FPU used):
- FP operations: Similar latencies to integer operations
- Single-cycle latencies for most computations except multiply and divide

VALIDATION_STATUS:
- ✓ Integer simple: 1 cycle - MATCHES
- ✗ Multiply: 3 cycles - DISCREPANCY (code says 4 cycles)
- ✗ Divide: 6-16 cycles worst case 16 - DISCREPANCY (code says 34 cycles)
- ✗ Load: 3 cycles - DISCREPANCY (code says 4 cycles latency)
- ✗ Store: 3 cycles - DISCREPANCY (code says 4 cycles latency)

[CHAPTER-7-PIPELINE]
UID: CH7-PIPELINE

TITLE: Pipeline Stages

LOCATION: Chapter 7.2, Figure 7-2

STAGES:
1. Fetch 0 - Instruction fetch stage 0
2. Fetch 1 - Instruction fetch stage 1
3. Decode - Instruction decode/dispatch stage
4. Execute 0 - Instruction execution stage 0
5. Execute 1 - Instruction execution stage 1 (feed forward)
6. Execute 2 - Instruction execution stage 2 (feed forward)
7. Write Back - Result write back to registers

VALIDATION_STATUS: ✓ MATCHES (partially)
- Code has: IF, ID, EX, MEM, WB (5 stages modeled)
- Manual has: IF0, IF1, DECODE, EX0, EX1, EX2, WB (7 stages)
- Note: Code simplifies to 5 stages, manual shows detailed 7-stage with dual fetch
- Memory access occurs in MEM stage (e200z6 has separate MEM stage, unlike e200z0)

[CHAPTER-5-INTERRUPTS]
UID: CH5-INTERRUPTS

TITLE: Interrupt Handling

LOCATION: Chapter 5.6 (Interrupt Definitions)

CRITICAL_INTERRUPT (IVOR0):
- Uses CSRR0/CSRR1 (Critical Save/Restore Registers)
- Hardware automatically saves:
  - CSRR0: Instruction address
  - CSRR1: MSR contents
- Return instruction: RFCI (Return From Critical Interrupt)

EXTERNAL_INTERRUPT (IVOR4):
- Should use SRR0/SRR1 (Standard Save/Restore Registers)
- Hardware automatically saves:
  - SRR0: Instruction address (if external interrupt)
  - SRR1: MSR contents (if external interrupt)
- Return instruction: RFI (Return From Interrupt)

NOTE: e200z6 manual confirms same pattern as e200z0 and e200z4:
- Critical interrupts use CSRR0/CSRR1 → RFCI
- External interrupts use SRR0/SRR1 → RFI

VALIDATION_STATUS: ✓ ALREADY IMPLEMENTED
LLVM_CURRENT_STATE: Interrupt type differentiation implemented in PPCFrameLowering.cpp
(shared code for all e200 cores) - verified working for e200z6

[CRITICAL-DISCREPANCIES]
UID: DISCREPANCIES

DISCREPANCY_001: Multiply Instruction Latency
Manual: 3 cycles
Code: 4 cycles (PPCScheduleE200Z6.td:97-102)
Impact: WCET analysis will be pessimistic (33% slower)
Priority: HIGH

DISCREPANCY_002: Divide Instruction Latency  
Manual: 6-16 cycles (worst case 16 cycles)
Code: 34 cycles (PPCScheduleE200Z6.td:90-94)
Impact: WCET analysis will be highly pessimistic (2.1x slower)
Priority: CRITICAL

DISCREPANCY_003: Load Instruction Latency
Manual: 3 cycles
Code: 4 cycles latency comment (PPCScheduleE200Z6.td:165-170)
Impact: WCET analysis will be pessimistic
Priority: HIGH

DISCREPANCY_004: Store Instruction Latency
Manual: 3 cycles
Code: 4 cycles latency comment (PPCScheduleE200Z6.td:188-192)
Impact: WCET analysis will be pessimistic
Priority: HIGH

